# ESeq instrument, effect and sequencer authoring

The full guide is `{{USER_ROOT}}/AGENTS.md`. Read it before writing anything and
follow its workflow. It lists where to write files, the rules files for
instruments and effects, factory examples, and the check command:

```sh
"{{ESEQ}}" instrument check "{{USER_INSTRUMENTS}}/<Name>"
"{{ESEQ}}" effect check "{{USER_EFFECTS}}/<Name>"
```

Write new instruments under `{{USER_INSTRUMENTS}}` and effects under
`{{USER_EFFECTS}}`, one folder each holding `dsp.lisp` and `ui.lisp`. Write
sequencers as Lisp modules under `{{LOCAL_PACKAGES}}` and check them with
`"{{ESEQ}}" sequencer check <module>`. Run the check until it prints `PASS`,
then open the PNG it prints and look at it.

If `{{USER_ROOT}}/AGENTS.md` is missing, start ESeq once; it writes the guide
when it launches.
